{"release":{"id":393948704,"tag":"3.14.0","author":"mmossg","name":"3.14.0","draft":false,"prerelease":false,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T08:22:53Z","publishedAt":"2026-09-22T16:52:58Z","markdown":"# Version 3.14.0 (September 22, 2026)\r\n\r\n## General\r\n\r\n1. [`458189298`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/458189298) Added the `ipc` [flag](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#option-flag-ipc), an experimental contact mode of the `discrete`\r\n   integrator for penetration-free flex contact. Each step minimizes an incremental potential subject to linearized\r\n   contact constraints, using a barrier-free augmented Lagrangian whose subproblems are the discrete solve. Every\r\n   committed position update is verified intersection-free by continuous collision detection, so flex contact cannot\r\n   tunnel. Supported for dim-2 flexes: a flex with edge equality constraints keeps its elasticity in the constraint\r\n   solver, while `elastic2d` elasticity is integrated implicitly through the effective metric. The contacts the mode\r\n   resolves are frictionless. The mode keeps contact multipliers across steps that no state specification covers, so\r\n   `mj_getState`/`mj_setState` do not capture its full state and exact replay is not supported.\r\n\r\n2. [`2fec92237`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/2fec92237) Introduced [archive resource providers](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjp_registerArchiveResourceProvider)\r\n   (`mjp_registerArchiveResourceProvider`). Archive providers use the\r\n   [`mjpResourceProvider`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjpResourceProvider) interface to mount and read archive containers (such as\r\n   `.mjz`/`.zip`), decoupling container handling from format decoders and enabling\r\n   on-demand asset extraction without requiring a pre-allocated [VFS](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#Virtualfilesystem).\r\n\r\n3. [`e312ce82d`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/e312ce82d) [Frames](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#frame) are now preserved when saving MJCF: `<frame>` elements are written with\r\n   their `pos` and `quat` and their contents in frame-relative coordinates, so a saved model reloads with the same\r\n   frames. Previously the frame transformation was accumulated into the children on save and only the frame's name was\r\n   kept. Changes to the `pos` or `quat` of a frame in an [`mjSpec`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjSpec) now also take effect when the spec is\r\n   recompiled.\r\n\r\n## Engine\r\n\r\n> [!WARNING]\r\n> **Breaking API changes**\r\n>\r\n> 4. [`dc8bb1364`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/dc8bb1364) [`mj_readCtrl`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_readCtrl) now matches the signature and semantics of [`mj_readSensor`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_readSensor) to support\r\n>    multi-input actuators (e.g., [pid](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-pid), [dcmotor](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-dcmotor),\r\n>    [orientation](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-orientation)): it takes an output buffer `result` of size `actuator_ctrlnum[id]`\r\n>    and returns `const mjtNum*` (a pointer into `mjData.ctrl` or `mjData.history` on zero-order-hold or exact\r\n>    timestamp matches, or `NULL` when interpolated values are written to `result`). Actuator history buffers now\r\n>    store `actuator_ctrlnum[id]` values per sample, and [`mj_initCtrlHistory`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_initCtrlHistory) expects `nsample *\r\n>    actuator_ctrlnum[id]` values ([#3597](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/3597)).\r\n\r\n5. [`9e0c6b577`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/9e0c6b577) The [mjWARN_INERTIA](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjtWarning) warning is now also raised by the modified-inertia\r\n   factorizations of the `implicitfast` and damped-`Euler` integrators (previously silent) and of the\r\n   `implicit` integrator (previously a fatal error).\r\n\r\n6. [`35c0631de`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/35c0631de) The sparse Newton solver no longer aborts with a \"rank-deficient sparse Hessian\" error when\r\n   rounding loses a pivot of its Hessian, as can happen in single precision with ill-conditioned inertia. The pivot is\r\n   now clamped and its row decoupled, as in the dense factorization.\r\n\r\n## Bug fixes\r\n\r\n7. [`2a3f1f5a4`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/2a3f1f5a4) Procedural model editing is no longer quadratic in the number of elements. `mjSpec` previously\r\n   recomputed the compilation signature on every [`mjs_addGeom`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_addGeom)-like call, and [`mjs_setName`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_setName) rescanned every\r\n   name of the element's type. Both are now incremental. Building a spec with 8000 geoms is roughly 10x faster.\r\n\r\n> [!WARNING]\r\n> **Breaking API changes**\r\n>\r\n> `mjsElement.signature` is now `0` whenever the spec has been structurally edited since it was last compiled,\r\n> rather than being eagerly recomputed on each edit. It is still equal to `mjModel.signature` after a successful\r\n> [`mj_compile`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_compile), which is what [`mj_copyBack`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mj_copyBack) and the Python `bind` methods rely on. Code that compared the\r\n> signature of an uncompiled spec against anything other than `0` must compile first. Additionally, when\r\n> [`mjs_setName`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_setName) fails on a duplicate name, the element's previous name is now preserved rather than being\r\n> overwritten with the duplicate name.\r\n\r\n8. [`ac329bd17`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/ac329bd17) Fixed the torque applied by [weld](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#equality-weld) constraints in\r\n   [`mj_rnePostConstraint`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_rnePostConstraint). The rotational constraint force was used directly as a world-frame torque, missing the\r\n   scaling by `0.5 * torquescale` and the rotation into the world frame. [Force](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-force) and\r\n   [torque](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-torque) sensors on bodies held by a weld that carries torque were wrong ([#2533](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/2533)).\r\n\r\n9. [`263c638c0`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/263c638c0) [`mj_rnePostConstraint`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_rnePostConstraint) now accounts for the forces of spatial tendons (spring, damper,\r\n   actuator, limit, friction loss, equality and armature), so [force](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-force) and\r\n   [torque](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-torque) sensors register the forces that tendons apply to bodies ([#832](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/832)).\r\n\r\n10. [`eb662fcaf`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/eb662fcaf) Tendon [actuatorfrclimited](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#tendon-spatial-actuatorfrclimited) now defaults to \"auto\" as\r\n    documented. Previously the default was \"false\" and `actuatorfrcrange` was silently ignored unless\r\n    `actuatorfrclimited` was set explicitly.\r\n\r\n11. [`54be9cce6`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/54be9cce6) [`mjd_transitionFD`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mjd_transitionFD) and [`mjd_inverseFD`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mjd_inverseFD) now raise an error when\r\n    [sleeping](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/computation/index.html#Sleeping) is enabled. Previously, their repeated evaluations changed the sleep state, leading to\r\n    internal errors or wrong derivatives.\r\n\r\n12. [`e38573c64`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/e38573c64) Fixed a memory leak in [`mjs_delete`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_delete) where deleted elements and subtrees were retained in\r\n    `mjSpec` until [`mj_deleteSpec`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mj_deleteSpec) ([#2882](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/2882)).\r\n\r\n13. [`65ea54c3c`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/65ea54c3c) Fixed an out-of-bounds read when parsing the header of a [GMSH file](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/search.html?q=gmsh-file-docs) loaded\r\n    by [flexcomp](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#body-flexcomp). Truncated headers are now reported as an error.\r\n","html":"<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h1 class=\"heading-element\">Version 3.14.0 (September 22, 2026)</h1><a id=\"user-content-version-3140-september-22-2026\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Version 3.14.0 (September 22, 2026)\" href=\"#version-3140-september-22-2026\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\">General</h2><a id=\"user-content-general\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: General\" href=\"#general\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/458189298\"><code>458189298</code></a> Added the <code>ipc</code> <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#option-flag-ipc\" rel=\"nofollow\">flag</a>, an experimental contact mode of the <code>discrete</code>\nintegrator for penetration-free flex contact. Each step minimizes an incremental potential subject to linearized\ncontact constraints, using a barrier-free augmented Lagrangian whose subproblems are the discrete solve. Every\ncommitted position update is verified intersection-free by continuous collision detection, so flex contact cannot\ntunnel. Supported for dim-2 flexes: a flex with edge equality constraints keeps its elasticity in the constraint\nsolver, while <code>elastic2d</code> elasticity is integrated implicitly through the effective metric. The contacts the mode\nresolves are frictionless. The mode keeps contact multipliers across steps that no state specification covers, so\n<code>mj_getState</code>/<code>mj_setState</code> do not capture its full state and exact replay is not supported.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/2fec92237\"><code>2fec92237</code></a> Introduced <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjp_registerArchiveResourceProvider\" rel=\"nofollow\">archive resource providers</a>\n(<code>mjp_registerArchiveResourceProvider</code>). Archive providers use the\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjpResourceProvider\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjpResourceProvider</code></a> interface to mount and read archive containers (such as\n<code>.mjz</code>/<code>.zip</code>), decoupling container handling from format decoders and enabling\non-demand asset extraction without requiring a pre-allocated <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#Virtualfilesystem\" rel=\"nofollow\">VFS</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/e312ce82d\"><code>e312ce82d</code></a> <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#frame\" rel=\"nofollow\">Frames</a> are now preserved when saving MJCF: <code>&lt;frame&gt;</code> elements are written with\ntheir <code>pos</code> and <code>quat</code> and their contents in frame-relative coordinates, so a saved model reloads with the same\nframes. Previously the frame transformation was accumulated into the children on save and only the frame's name was\nkept. Changes to the <code>pos</code> or <code>quat</code> of a frame in an <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjSpec\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjSpec</code></a> now also take effect when the spec is\nrecompiled.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\">Engine</h2><a id=\"user-content-engine\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Engine\" href=\"#engine\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[!WARNING]\n<strong>Breaking API changes</strong></p>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/dc8bb1364\"><code>dc8bb1364</code></a> <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_readCtrl\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_readCtrl</code></a> now matches the signature and semantics of <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_readSensor\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_readSensor</code></a> to support\nmulti-input actuators (e.g., <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-pid\" rel=\"nofollow\">pid</a>, <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-dcmotor\" rel=\"nofollow\">dcmotor</a>,\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-orientation\" rel=\"nofollow\">orientation</a>): it takes an output buffer <code>result</code> of size <code>actuator_ctrlnum[id]</code>\nand returns <code>const mjtNum*</code> (a pointer into <code>mjData.ctrl</code> or <code>mjData.history</code> on zero-order-hold or exact\ntimestamp matches, or <code>NULL</code> when interpolated values are written to <code>result</code>). Actuator history buffers now\nstore <code>actuator_ctrlnum[id]</code> values per sample, and <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_initCtrlHistory\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_initCtrlHistory</code></a> expects <code>nsample * actuator_ctrlnum[id]</code> values (<a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/3597\">#3597</a>).</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<ol start=\"5\">\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/9e0c6b577\"><code>9e0c6b577</code></a> The <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjtWarning\" rel=\"nofollow\">mjWARN_INERTIA</a> warning is now also raised by the modified-inertia\nfactorizations of the <code>implicitfast</code> and damped-<code>Euler</code> integrators (previously silent) and of the\n<code>implicit</code> integrator (previously a fatal error).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/35c0631de\"><code>35c0631de</code></a> The sparse Newton solver no longer aborts with a \"rank-deficient sparse Hessian\" error when\nrounding loses a pivot of its Hessian, as can happen in single precision with ill-conditioned inertia. The pivot is\nnow clamped and its row decoupled, as in the dense factorization.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\">Bug fixes</h2><a id=\"user-content-bug-fixes\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Bug fixes\" href=\"#bug-fixes\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ol start=\"7\">\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/2a3f1f5a4\"><code>2a3f1f5a4</code></a> Procedural model editing is no longer quadratic in the number of elements. <code>mjSpec</code> previously\nrecomputed the compilation signature on every <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_addGeom\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjs_addGeom</code></a>-like call, and <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_setName\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjs_setName</code></a> rescanned every\nname of the element's type. Both are now incremental. Building a spec with 8000 geoms is roughly 10x faster.</li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[!WARNING]\n<strong>Breaking API changes</strong></p>\n<p><code>mjsElement.signature</code> is now <code>0</code> whenever the spec has been structurally edited since it was last compiled,\nrather than being eagerly recomputed on each edit. It is still equal to <code>mjModel.signature</code> after a successful\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_compile\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_compile</code></a>, which is what <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mj_copyBack\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_copyBack</code></a> and the Python <code>bind</code> methods rely on. Code that compared the\nsignature of an uncompiled spec against anything other than <code>0</code> must compile first. Additionally, when\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_setName\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjs_setName</code></a> fails on a duplicate name, the element's previous name is now preserved rather than being\noverwritten with the duplicate name.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<ol start=\"8\">\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/ac329bd17\"><code>ac329bd17</code></a> Fixed the torque applied by <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#equality-weld\" rel=\"nofollow\">weld</a> constraints in\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_rnePostConstraint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_rnePostConstraint</code></a>. The rotational constraint force was used directly as a world-frame torque, missing the\nscaling by <code>0.5 * torquescale</code> and the rotation into the world frame. <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-force\" rel=\"nofollow\">Force</a> and\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-torque\" rel=\"nofollow\">torque</a> sensors on bodies held by a weld that carries torque were wrong (<a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/2533\">#2533</a>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/263c638c0\"><code>263c638c0</code></a> <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mj_rnePostConstraint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_rnePostConstraint</code></a> now accounts for the forces of spatial tendons (spring, damper,\nactuator, limit, friction loss, equality and armature), so <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-force\" rel=\"nofollow\">force</a> and\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-torque\" rel=\"nofollow\">torque</a> sensors register the forces that tendons apply to bodies (<a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/832\">#832</a>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/eb662fcaf\"><code>eb662fcaf</code></a> Tendon <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#tendon-spatial-actuatorfrclimited\" rel=\"nofollow\">actuatorfrclimited</a> now defaults to \"auto\" as\ndocumented. Previously the default was \"false\" and <code>actuatorfrcrange</code> was silently ignored unless\n<code>actuatorfrclimited</code> was set explicitly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/54be9cce6\"><code>54be9cce6</code></a> <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mjd_transitionFD\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjd_transitionFD</code></a> and <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions_override.html#mjd_inverseFD\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjd_inverseFD</code></a> now raise an error when\n<a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/computation/index.html#Sleeping\" rel=\"nofollow\">sleeping</a> is enabled. Previously, their repeated evaluations changed the sleep state, leading to\ninternal errors or wrong derivatives.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/e38573c64\"><code>e38573c64</code></a> Fixed a memory leak in <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mjs_delete\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mjs_delete</code></a> where deleted elements and subtrees were retained in\n<code>mjSpec</code> until <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mj_deleteSpec\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>mj_deleteSpec</code></a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/2882\">#2882</a>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/65ea54c3c\"><code>65ea54c3c</code></a> Fixed an out-of-bounds read when parsing the header of a <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/search.html?q=gmsh-file-docs\" rel=\"nofollow\">GMSH file</a> loaded\nby <a href=\"https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#body-flexcomp\" rel=\"nofollow\">flexcomp</a>. Truncated headers are now reported as an error.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n","assets":[{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":32814642,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:42Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:45Z","downloadCount":84,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-linux-aarch64.tar.gz"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":101,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:45Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:45Z","downloadCount":18,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-linux-aarch64.tar.gz.sha256"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":33314907,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:39Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:41Z","downloadCount":268,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":100,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:42Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:42Z","downloadCount":66,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz.sha256"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":52504358,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:49Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:51Z","downloadCount":1015,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-macos-universal2.dmg"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":101,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:52Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:52Z","downloadCount":13,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-macos-universal2.dmg.sha256"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":22109742,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:46Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:48Z","downloadCount":461,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-windows-x86_64.zip"},{"contentType":"application/octet-stream","size":99,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:48Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T16:51:48Z","downloadCount":81,"downloadUrl":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/releases/download/3.14.0/mujoco-3.14.0-windows-x86_64.zip.sha256"}]}}